# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
*.key
*.pem

# --- Experiment output: DENY BY DEFAULT ----------------------------------------
# Raw measurement records are gitignored on purpose. They are regenerable from
# run.py + manifest.json, they get large, and in eval work they can contain
# material you should not redistribute. Everything a reader needs to check your
# arithmetic is in summary.json and RESULTS.md, both of which ARE committed.
#
# WHY DENY-BY-DEFAULT AND NOT A LIST OF DIRECTORIES:
# The rule this replaces enumerated directory NAMES — output/acts/,
# output/acts_verify/. A third directory, acts_axes/, was created later in the
# sprint, matched none of them, and put 894 MB of raw activation tensors into git
# history. It surfaced only when the first push to a public remote hung, and
# recovery meant git-filter-repo and a force-push, under deadline pressure.
#
# An allowlist cannot have that failure mode. Anything new under an output
# directory is ignored the moment it is created, whatever it is called; the
# small derived artifacts that constitute the evidence are named explicitly
# below. Adding a new kind of evidence is a deliberate one-line edit here —
# which is the correct amount of friction, given what the alternative cost.
experiments/**/output*/**

# The evidence. Small, derived, human-checkable, committed.
!experiments/**/output*/summary.json
!experiments/**/output*/manifest.json
!experiments/**/output*/RESULTS.md

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Models and large local caches ---------------------------------------------
models/
checkpoints/
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.bin

# --- Rendered output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Paper SOURCE is committed; the rendered PDF is a build artifact.
writeup/*.pdf

# The Typst intermediate that scripts/build_paper.py generates from the Markdown.
# Named `.generated.typ` rather than `.typ` so this rule cannot swallow a Typst
# file someone wrote by hand and intends as their source.
writeup/*.generated.typ

# --- OS -----------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
